SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

What the program carries inside itself. `glib-compile-resources` turns this
and the `greeting.ui` that blueprint-compiler produced into a C file of bytes,
which is compiled and linked in like any other -- so the finished binary has
no markup to find at run time and no directory it has to be started from.

The prefix is the application ID written as a path, which is the convention,
and it is the first half of the resource path `greeting.c` hands to
`gtk_widget_class_set_template_from_resource`.
-->
<gresources>
  <gresource prefix="/dev/jcollie/fluent/Greeting">
    <file>greeting.ui</file>
  </gresource>
</gresources>
